# Best practices

## Code
- TypeScript strict. No `any`, no `@ts-ignore`, no `eslint-disable` to silence real issues.
- Function components + hooks only. Keep components small; one component per file in `src/components/`.
- Personal content lives only in `src/data/*.ts` as typed data. Components never hard-code bio text, links or project facts.
- Styling via Tailwind utilities and tokens defined in `src/styles/index.css` (`@theme`). No inline hex colors in components.
- Prefer CSS for animation; use `motion` only where CSS can't. Every animation respects `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Lazy-load routes that are not the home page. Avoid adding dependencies unless they clearly beat ~50 lines of code.
- Clean up effects (event listeners, rAF, observers) on unmount.

## Accessibility
- Semantic landmarks (`header`, `nav`, `main`, `section` with headings, `footer`), one `h1` per route.
- Every interactive element is keyboard reachable with a visible focus style. Use `button` for actions, `a` for navigation.
- Decorative canvas/visuals get `aria-hidden="true"`. Images have meaningful `alt` or `alt=""` if decorative.
- Text contrast >= WCAG AA.

## Performance
- Keep the initial JS bundle small. No large animation/3D libraries. Self-host fonts (`@fontsource`), `font-display: swap`.
- Canvas effects pause when off-screen or tab hidden, and are throttled to rAF.

## Testing
- Each section/page has a Vitest + Testing Library smoke test (renders, key text/links present, a11y-relevant roles).
- `npm run check` must pass before a task is considered done.

## Git
- Conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `refactor:`). One task per commit.
